question:
In mobile-first design, where are tablet/desktop styles defined?
```css
/* Base mobile styles */
.container { width: 100%; }

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .container { width: 80%; }
}
```

What will this media query match?
```css
@media (min-width: 600px) and (max-width: 900px) {
  .box { width: 50%; }
}
```

How will a device with pixel ratio 2 (retina) match this?
```css
@media (min-device-pixel-ratio: 2) {
  .icon { background-image: url('icon-2x.png'); }
}
```

When would prefers-color-scheme be applied?
```css
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  body { background: #1a1a1a; color: #fff; }
}
```

Which is the correct syntax for multiple conditions with OR logic?
```css
@media (max-width: 600px), (max-width: 900px) { }
@media (max-width: 600px) or (max-width: 900px) { }
@media (max-width: 600px) | (max-width: 900px) { }
```

What is the difference between width and device-width in media queries?
```css
@media (min-width: 768px) { } /* viewport width */
@media (min-device-width: 768px) { } /* device screen width */
```

In this media query range, what viewport widths will match?
```css
@media (width: 768px) { .box { width: 50%; } }
```

How do feature queries differ from media queries?
```css
@supports (display: grid) { .container { display: grid; } }
```

